{"timestamp":"2026-08-06T02:07:05.708Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_044b9c7c4d3e7db0016a73ec459b20819187c1417faa4f1e13","status":"completed","call_id":"call_2SGLt5bwuWpWgR6sGlsIoQka","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({\"cmd\":\"jq '{count: (.branches|length), needsRebase: ([.branches[]|select(.needsRebase)]|length), first: .branches[0].name, last: .branches[-1].name, currentBranch}' /tmp/evorto-current-stack.json && sed -n '1,260p' /tmp/evorto-pr124-source-replay-final/MANIFEST.md\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":5000});\ntext(r.output);","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019fd2d8-aa27-7b33-9da1-34e7e79b653d"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-06T02:07:05.828Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_019fd4d3-0064-7870-9445-3dceda2d3534","call_id":"call_2SGLt5bwuWpWgR6sGlsIoQka","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\n  \"count\": 80,\n  \"needsRebase\": 0,\n  \"first\": \"codex/remove-prior-compliance-artifacts\",\n  \"last\": \"codex/target-information-only-events-by-role\",\n  \"currentBranch\": \"codex/target-information-only-events-by-role\"\n}\n# PR124 latency replay manifest\n\nThis directory contains the audited four-commit PR124 patch series. The series\nwas reconstructed in an isolated clone; it did not change the shared Evorto\nworktree, shared refs, remotes, containers, or databases.\n\n## Replay boundary\n\n- Validated parent commit: `3e8dba22dc004618bddcfddc3b55b21df90a1dd6`\n- Validated parent tree: `d53722018121f79a207673c2bb6ca9561f6fb0b8`\n- Source-series tip: `2c9e5d12b9bfa7e9dd9e90638b659ef8da26b7a1`\n- Source-series final tree: `6291716e1b6e6ee45ae367ae1e3f9df7b7c9625d`\n- Aggregate diff: 16 unique files, 1,679 additions, 106 deletions\n\nThe patch series must ultimately be applied after the final PR123 tip and its\none-file `APPLICATION_REVIEW_QUEUE.md` closure branch. PR124 does not touch that\nqueue file, but the exact-tree proof below applies only to the validated parent\nlisted above. Replay these patches on the final parent, resolve any later\nUI/Docker overlap in favor of the final PR123 behavior, and re-run the integrated\ngates before publishing branches.\n\n## Commits and patches\n\n| # | Subject | Source commit | Result tree | Files | Add | Del | Patch SHA-256 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n| 1 | `perf: trace staging request latency` | `d3d98363e4a0cdd15a001b436fe2a749c59535a6` | `eb18384b2fe1bf5b63d05a8d27db70d02168fb50` | 7 | 195 | 105 | `ae58dace0f7e873a85b55779d1c647efabac5185a5adba264d20709afe07c608` |\n| 2 | `feat: add bounded staging latency probe` | `73b03ecb0e63b8a5433368b87a6273da2b59bf0b` | `3e9b5b6b90e4d424a6d5e452ebb5b6afbf3e6e3b` | 2 | 764 | 0 | `6dacd4153c1f8307005d7ce8ce9941b9caee169afffd4ff21fdbf03cae794775` |\n| 3 | `ci: automate staging latency evidence` | `cc948f6c252be944bdf132f531d318191b1b0211` | `910c970b761c846e658c81904ad66127080d69c3` | 3 | 112 | 1 | `769f1cf4150d35d304422429539460de62425c0fc82cf594e37bfd6f4c7f7cd5` |\n| 4 | `docs: explain staging latency response` | `2c9e5d12b9bfa7e9dd9e90638b659ef8da26b7a1` | `6291716e1b6e6ee45ae367ae1e3f9df7b7c9625d` | 5 | 608 | 0 | `b2acffcaeb73a719a94213ed78f208c3afe0f9e7bd3616b2308c680390a59e5d` |\n\nEvery commit is below 100 files and 1,500 changed lines. Commit 2 is a\nstandalone, directly runnable probe with its own fixture-backed checks; commit 3\nthen schedules and records it.\n\n## Audit corrections\n\n- Patch 1 originally conflicted with newer request-context and event-discovery\n  work. The replay preserves the lower stack's permission partitioning,\n  warnings, role-targeted discovery, and single-query `userRegistered` result;\n  it adds only the bounded trace spans and annotations.\n- The change note was narrowed to the behavior delivered by patch 1 and uses\n  plain product language. Its forbidden-term scan is clean.\n- Patch 3 originally referred to nonexistent `steps.ops` and `steps.traffic`\n  outputs. The invalid condition was removed because this deployment job has no\n  scheduled trigger and reaches the probe only after the release smoke checks.\n  Two source assertions prevent those stale references from returning.\n- The operational guidance now consistently says that every successful staging\n  deployment retains the ten-sample report-only baseline.\n\n## Verification\n\nAll checks ran in `/tmp/evorto-pr124-source-replay.cAdiFR/repo` without local\nservices:\n\n- `bun run format:write` — passed on the final content.\n- `bun run lint` — passed.\n- Focused eight-file server/helper run — 8 files, 61 tests passed.\n- `bun run test:unit:server` — 187 files, 1,489 tests passed with no incomplete\n  outcomes.\n- `bash -n ops/scaleway/probe-http-latency.sh` — passed.\n- `actionlint .github/workflows/staging-latency.yml .github/workflows/scaleway-staging.yml`\n  — passed after correcting the stale outputs.\n- `bun run build:app` — passed, including all four operations bundles.\n- `git diff --check` — clean.\n- The changed change note contains none of the prohibited implementation terms.\n\nAn independent clone at\n`/tmp/evorto-pr124-independent-replay-final.5Al6s8/repo` applied the four exported\npatches from the validated parent with `git am`, without conflicts. Its tree\nafter each patch exactly matched the four result trees above; its final tree was\n`6291716e1b6e6ee45ae367ae1e3f9df7b7c9625d`, and its worktree was clean.\n\n## Apply in order\n\n```sh\ngit am \\\n  /tmp/evorto-pr124-source-replay-final/0001-perf-trace-staging-request-latency.patch \\\n  /tmp/evorto-pr124-source-replay-final/0002-feat-add-bounded-staging-latency-probe.patch \\\n  /tmp/evorto-pr124-source-replay-final/0003-ci-automate-staging-latency-evidence.patch \\\n  /tmp/evorto-pr124-source-replay-final/0004-docs-explain-staging-latency-response.patch\n```\n\nThe source commit IDs are local detached-clone objects. Treat the exported patch\nfiles, their hashes, and the result-tree sequence as the durable handoff.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019fd2d8-aa27-7b33-9da1-34e7e79b653d"}}}
