{"timestamp":"2026-08-06T02:08:35.374Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_044b9c7c4d3e7db0016a73eca09de08191b049c8d3a176fa0c","status":"completed","call_id":"call_SB9ZbLc4CR4pBAvZsf45Sycj","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({\"cmd\":\"sha256sum /tmp/evorto-review-queue-source-3e8dba22/0001-docs-add-application-review-queue.patch && git apply --check --whitespace=error-all /tmp/evorto-review-queue-source-3e8dba22/0001-docs-add-application-review-queue.patch && git apply --stat /tmp/evorto-review-queue-source-3e8dba22/0001-docs-add-application-review-queue.patch && git apply --numstat /tmp/evorto-review-queue-source-3e8dba22/0001-docs-add-application-review-queue.patch && sed -n '1,320p' /tmp/evorto-review-queue-source-3e8dba22/0001-docs-add-application-review-queue.patch\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":20000});\ntext(r.output);","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019fd2d8-aa27-7b33-9da1-34e7e79b653d"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-06T02:08:35.518Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_019fd4d4-5ebe-7b91-834c-4837c8c872f3","call_id":"call_SB9ZbLc4CR4pBAvZsf45Sycj","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 10036)\nTotal output lines: 249\n\n8fca57ab7b641536c0fcc9bf8d83d0cb52bc37d8761a9df753a0be9c327f32ad  /tmp/evorto-review-queue-source-3e8dba22/0001-docs-add-application-review-queue.patch\n APPLICATION_REVIEW_QUEUE.md |  239 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n 1 file changed, 239 insertions(+)\n239\t0\tAPPLICATION_REVIEW_QUEUE.md\ndiff --git a/APPLICATION_REVIEW_QUEUE.md b/APPLICATION_REVIEW_QUEUE.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..d0213e7\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/APPLICATION_REVIEW_QUEUE.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,239 @@\n+# Application Review Queue\n+\n+Updated: 2026-08-06\n+\n+Review baseline: `origin/main` at\n+`d117229d3d7d357af9f9fc61fdad8d348d6809ea`\n+\n+Prepared source checkpoint:\n+`3e8dba22dc004618bddcfddc3b55b21df90a1dd6`\n+\n+Intended closure branch: `codex/full-application-simplification-review`\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Leave one safe, direct application that a single developer can understand and\n+maintain. The review covers defects, incomplete behavior, inconsistent product\n+rules, security boundaries, avoidable complexity, hidden failures, and stale\n+code.\n+\n+The application will start from a fresh schema. It has no product requirement\n+for old-schema compatibility or alternate behavior that makes a failed\n+operation look successful.\n+\n+## Review rules\n+\n+- Prefer one obvious implementation and delete obsolete alternatives.\n+- Surface unexpected failures. Do not replace them with guessed data, silent\n+  empty results, automatic retries, or a second path.\n+- Keep money, capacity, authorization, identity, tenant, and file boundaries\n+  explicit on the server.\n+- Keep required concurrency and payment safeguards, but do not generalize\n+  distinct workflows merely to share orchestration.\n+- Use defaults only when creating a new record. Invalid stored state must fail\n+  visibly.\n+- Keep application screens, emails, and generated product guides in plain\n+  product language. Service names, identifiers, transport details, test\n+  evidence, and diagnostics stay out of user-facing copy.\n+- A coverage row is complete only when its current-tree evidence is complete.\n+  Source completion and environment-backed proof are recorded separately.\n+\n+## Status meanings\n+\n+- **Complete**: review, implementation, and the required current evidence are\n+  complete.\n+- **In progress**: the direction is settled and a bounded implementation or\n+  verification batch remains.\n+- **Resolved**: the named finding or simplification was implemented with\n+  focused evidence.\n+- **Accepted**: the remaining complexity protects a documented invariant and\n+  has a narrow boundary.\n+- **Blocked**: an exact external prerequisite prevents required proof. Weaker\n+  evidence is not substituted.\n+\n+## Current checkpoint\n+\n+The source reconstruction contains 80 focused commits over the review\n+baseline. It changes 692 files in aggregate because it removes the old schema,\n+migration, and compatibility surfaces while rebuilding the supported product\n+flows. Those aggregate numbers describe the stack, not one pull request.\n+\n+Evidence already completed on the exact prepared source checkpoint:\n+\n+- `bun run format:write` passed.\n+- `bun run lint` passed.\n+- The focused release-source checks passed 4/4.\n+- The complete server unit suite passed 186/186 files and 1,484/1,484 tests,\n+  with no incomplete tests.\n+- `bun run build:app` passed for the browser, server-rendered application, and\n+  operations bundles.\n+\n+The application unit suite is not yet a passing checkpoint. It currently has\n+127/133 files and 950/961 tests passing; 11 failures in six files belong to the\n+pending UI replay. This is an open proof item, not an accepted failure.\n+\n+## Coverage queue\n+\n+| ID     | Area                                   | Status      | Current evidence and remaining proof                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |\n+| ------ | -------------------------------------- | ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n+| RQ-001 | Historical artifacts                   | Complete    | Prior scan/compliance output, the old migration implementation, and stale compatibility surfaces are removed. The user-cancelled automated scan was not restarted and is not claimed as evidence.                                                                |\n+| RQ-002 | Product and architecture               | In progress | D-003 is implemented in the source checkpoint: ordinary discovery derives from current option eligibility, templates carry structure only, and announcements retain their separate selected-role rule. Final UI, documentation, and Browser proof remain open.   |\n+| RQ-003 | Application shell and server rendering | In progress | Source boundaries, routing, identity, tenant resolution, and failure states were reviewed and rebuilt. The final UI replay, application suite, and Browser walkthrough remain open.                                                                              |\n+| RQ-004 | Events and templates                   | In progress | Obsolete ordinary event/template audience state and controls are deleted; server, UI, schema, public projection, direct-link, and structural-snapshot behavior implement D-003. Final application, PostgreSQL, Playwright, guide, and Browser proof remain open. |\n+| RQ-005 | Registration operations                | In progress | Registration graph integrity, add-ons, waitlists, questions, check-in, and eligibility writes are implemented and covered by the green server suite. PostgreSQL and full journeys remain open.                                                                   |\n+| RQ-006 | Transfers and payments                 | In progress | Private fixed-bundle claims, one registration/add-on Checkout, attachment of the first organization payment account, refund recovery, and write-time eligibility are implemented. PostgreSQL and provider-backed journeys remain open.                           |\n+| RQ-007 | Identity and administration            | In progress | Request identity, role authority, onboarding, focused settings, member administration, and profile identity rules are implemented. The final UI replay and Browser proof remain open.                                                                            |\n+| RQ-008 | Finance and notifications              | In progress | Receipt evidence, finance contracts and writes, reimbursements, views, and single-dispatch email behavior are implemented and included in the green server suite. PostgreSQL and journey proof remain open.                                                      |\n+| RQ-009 | Server and public operations           | Complete    | The exact checkpoint passes the full 1,484-test server suite and production build. Public failures remain plain while diagnostic context stays private.                                                                                                          |\n+| RQ-010 | Database                               | In progress | The fresh schema and ownership constraints are reconstructed without migration compatibility. The exact final PostgreSQL suite remains open.                                                                                                                     |\n+| RQ-011 | Operations                             | In progress | Forward-only deployment, isolated infrastructure state, explicit configuration, and hardened runtime-image source are present. The bounded Docker lifecycle patch and real lifecycle/image proof remain open.                                                    |\n+| RQ-012 | Tests and generated guides             | In progress | Test ownership, source guards, and guide rules were reviewed. The UI replay, complete application suite, functional/integration journeys, official guide publication, live provider checks, and final asset audit remain open.                                   |\n+| RQ-013 | Manual security review                 | Complete    | Authentication, authorization, tenant isolation, request ingress, uploads, redirects, caching, and server-rendered data exposure were manually traced. This is manual review evidence only.                                                                      |\n+| RQ-014 | Simplification review                  | Complete    | Forty-one candidates and their concrete simpler directions are retained below; 38 were simplified and three have explicit accepted boundaries.                                                                                                                   |\n+| RQ-015 | Final verification                     | In progress | Format, lint, release-source checks, full server unit, and production build pass on the exact source checkpoint. Application unit, Docker/image, PostgreSQL, Playwright/guides/providers, and branch-authentic Browser proof remain open.                        |\n+\n+## Findings queue\n+\n+The prior detailed queue contained 155 findings. This reconstruction preserves\n+their identifiers and outcomes, adds the bounded-Docker defect as F-157, and\n+adds the misleading unused event-discovery permission as F-158. Source fixes\n+are reconstructed; environment-dependent outcome claims stay open under the\n+coverage rows above.\n+\n+Current total: **157 findings** — 154 resolved in source, two accepted at\n+explicit boundaries (F-049 and F-125), and one in progress (F-157).\n+\n+| Area                                 | Finding IDs                                                                     | Source disposition                                                                                                           |\n+| ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n+| Critical boundaries                  | F-001–F-005                                                                     | Resolved in focused infrastructure, transfer, email, public-error, and receipt-storage slices.                               |\n+| Security, identity, and requests     | F-006–F-018, F-074, F-077–F-079, F-081, F-082, F-085, F-088–F-090, F-092, F-095 | Resolved in the source checkpoint; final user-flow proof is tracked separately.                                              |\n+| Events, templates, and registration  | F-019–F-032, F-071, F-075, F-076, F-080, F-083, F-084, F-086, F-087, F-091      | Resolved in source; PostgreSQL and full journey proof remain open.                                                           |\n+| Finance and notifications            | F-033–F-043                                                                     | Resolved in source; finance and email PostgreSQL/journey proof remains open.                                                 |\n+| Database and domain integrity        | F-044–F-049                                                                     | Resolved in the fresh schema; current PostgreSQL proof remains open.                                                         |\n+| Administration and experience        | F-050–F-055                                                                     | Resolved in source; the final UI replay and Browser proof remain open.                                                       |\n+| Operations, tests, and release       | F-056–F-064, F-093, F-094                                                       | Resolved in source except for the separate F-157 lifecycle work; runtime proof remains open.                                 |\n+| Removed compatibility and stale code | F-065–F-070, F-073                                                              | Resolved by deletion, without aliases or alternate legacy behavior.                                                          |\n+| Settled-decision follow-up           | F-096–F-156                                                                     | Source outcomes are reconstructed. Final UI, database, provider, guide, image, and Browser claims remain governed by RQ-015. |\n+\n+### Findings that must stay explicit\n+\n+| ID    | Severity | Finding                                                                                                                                                                                                                     | Required simple outcome                                                                                                                                                                                                   | Status                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n+| ----- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n+| F-020 | High     | Ordinary events and templates persisted a separately configured participant/organizer/both/unlisted audience, duplicating registration-option eligibility and allowing discovery to drift from who could actually register. | Delete ordinary event and template audience state; derive signed-in discovery from current option eligibility and anonymous discovery from options available to default roles, while rechecking every registration write. | Resolved in source: the audience enum, columns, contracts, controls, seed state, and compatibility paths are deleted; discovery and every registration boundary use current option eligibility. |\n+| F-152 | Medium   | Plain-language guards missed shared or composed visible copy and final generated output, allowing implementation wording to reach people using the product.                                                                 | Check visible application copy, public failures, every email variant, and final generated guide text. Fix the owning source; do not patch generated pages.                                                                | Resolved in source; the final generated-guide run remains open.                                                                                                                                 |\n+| F-157 | Medium   | Project-scoped Docker commands could wait indefinitely, leaving an apparently stuck development and verification environment with poor bounded diagnostics.                                                                 | Put only project-scoped lifecycle calls behind explicit time limits, fail with the exact command and diagnostics, and provide no retry loop, alternate stack, or broad Docker cleanup.                                    | In progress: the focused patch and its 47 tests are prepared, but it is not part of source checkpoint `3e8dba22`; final replay and real lifecycle proof remain open.                            |\n+| F-158 | Medium   | `events:viewPublic` was configurable even though no runtime path enforced it, and stale old-audience references made the discovery slice misleading.                                                                        | Delete the unused permission and every stale seed, test, and guide reference; do not preserve an alias or route ordinary discovery through announcement visibility.                                                       | Resolved in source: the permission and stale old-model references are removed in the option-derived discovery slice.                                                                            |\n+\n+## Complexity and simplification queue\n+\n+Every recommendation has a deletion test or a narrow retained boundary. A\n+file-only split is not a simplification.\n+\n+| ID or group | Candidate                                                                                                                                                                                                                        | Simpler direction                                                                                                                                                                 | Status                                                         |\n+| ----------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n+| C-001–C-005 | Old schema/importer, unsupported modes, duplicate transfer credentials/columns, and dead registration/payment paths                                                                                                              | Delete the parallel models and paths; keep only the current schema, one private claim, and canonical payment lifecycle.                                                           | Resolved                                                       |\n+| C-006       | Registration and transfer Checkout orchestration                                                                                                                                                                                 | Use one Checkout for a new registration and add-ons. Keep transfer as a fixed-bundle claim with its own refund and ambiguous-completion rules; share stable primitives only.      | Accepted                                                       |\n+| C-007–C-019 | Old event operations, broad handlers, request bridges, duplicate server/authority/finance logic, remote fan-out, outbox forwarding, automatic infrastructure recovery, and brittle test inventories                              | Delete dead surfaces; extract only policy reused at real transaction or authorization seams; keep orchestration local.                                                            | Resolved, except C-008 is accepted at its transaction boundary |\n+| C-020       | User profile mega-component                                                                                                                                                                                                      | Keep a small shell and give substantial areas routed pages that own their data; make the overview useful.                                                                         | Resolved                                                       |\n+| C-021       | General settings mega-form                                                                                                                                                                                                       | Use independently saved focused pages in the familiar two-column layout; keep payments restricted and delete the monolithic payload.                                              | Resolved             …36 tokens truncated…duplicate privacy truth, handler-specific defect stripping, unsupported payment rotation, dead tax helpers, and placeholder provider configuration | Delete unused state and use one authoritative read/write boundary for each supported concept.                                                                                     | Resolved                                                       |\n+| C-032       | Temporary Bun/Angular reported-version define                                                                                                                                                                                    | Keep the visible build-only constraint only until a stable Bun release carries the required Angular support, then delete it. Do not replace it with a canary production baseline. | Accepted, pending the separately reviewed Bun update           |\n+| C-033–C-036 | Rebuilt requests, oversized raw fixtures, settings pseudo-fallbacks, and an unused filesystem cache layer                                                                                                                        | Normalize once, keep narrow scenario fixtures, use one initialized-settings invariant, and delete unused runtime state.                                                           | Resolved                                                       |\n+| C-037       | Generic listing/visibility operation after ordinary audiences were removed                                                                                                                                                       | Rename the surviving surface to announcement discovery and delete the generic names without aliases; ordinary option-derived discovery must not route through it.                 | Resolved                                                       |\n+| C-038       | Generic error-message humanization                                                                                                                                                                                               | Delete message and error-name guessing. Each action owns one plain failure message; known recoverable states remain explicit and diagnostics remain private.                      | Resolved                                                       |\n+| C-039       | Brute-force runtime-port test                                                                                                                                                                                                    | Prove representative and boundary seeds instead of sampling thousands of values or increasing the timeout.                                                                        | Resolved                                                       |\n+| C-040–C-041 | Generated-guide compatibility pages, fragile screenshot coupling, and capture retries                                                                                                                                            | Keep one current destination, capture once after proving readiness, fail on unfinished content, and never patch generated output.                                                 | Source resolved; final publication proof remains open          |\n+\n+### Accepted complexity boundaries\n+\n+- Row locks, durable claims, idempotency keys, and explicit ambiguous-payment\n+  stops protect money and capacity. Simplify duplication around them, not the\n+  invariants.\n+- Registration plus add-ons and transfer share a review shape, but their\n+  post-payment ownership and recovery differ. Do not build a generic checkout\n+  framework merely to make the files look alike.\n+- Targeted platform operations retain explicit target, reason, permission, and\n+  audit boundaries.\n+- Typed public operations and tagged domain outcomes remain the one\n+  client/server contract.\n+- File signature checks, hashes, immutable object keys, and narrow signed links\n+  are required storage controls.\n+- The three current themes are product choices: the new `evorto` palette is the\n+  default, the previous Evorto palette remains `classic`, and `esn` remains\n+  selectable. They are not compatibility aliases.\n+\n+## Settled product decisions\n+\n+| ID    | Product boundary                         | Settled direction                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           | Source outcome                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  |\n+| ----- | ---------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n+| D-001 | Waitlists and active-registration limits | A waitlist entry does not consume the tenant active-registration limit. Check the limit only when converting it into a real registration.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | Implemented: waitlist joins remain lightweight; registration and transfer completion enforce the real limit.                                                                                                                                                    |\n+| D-002 | Participant registration transfer        | Keep one private offer-and-claim flow. A wholly free, questionless claim completes immediately; every payment-involving transfer remains asynchronous through Stripe.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       | Implemented: obsolete participant direct reassignment is deleted. The narrow organizer reassignment remains limited to a wholly free, no-refund, questionless bundle.                                                                                           |\n+| D-003 | Ordinary event and template discovery    | Ordinary optionful events have no separately configured listing audience, and templates define structure only with no discovery visibility or default audience. A signed-in member discovers a published event when currently eligible for at least one option; an anonymous visitor discovers it when an option is available to a role assigned by default to new users in that tenant and receives only the public projection. Discovery grants no access, every registration write rechecks eligibility, and direct-link ineligibility remains explicit. | Implemented in source: schema, contracts, authoring, seeds, server queries, public projection, direct-link states, and write boundaries use the option-derived rule without an audience compatibility path. Final integrated UI and journey proof remains open. |\n+| D-004 | Optionless announcement discovery        | Optionless announcements are intentionally separate from D-003: an explicit selected set of tenant roles controls normal visibility, an empty set means link-only, and the selection neither grants roles/access nor sends notifications.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | Implemented in source: event-owned role selection, empty-selection link-only behavior, role-deletion integrity, and announcement-specific operations remain separate from ordinary discovery. Final integrated UI and journey proof remains open.               |\n+| D-005 | Tenant settings structure                | General settings are independently saved focused pages inside the familiar two-column settings layout. Payment/provider configuration has its own restricted page; exact labels may stay product-design choices.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            | Implemented: organization, registration, appearance, legal, and payments have focused routes and writes; the monolith and tenant fallback are deleted.                                                                                                          |\n+| D-006 | Profile structure                        | Keep a small shared shell, move substantial areas to pages, and redesign the sparse overview into a meaningful landing page.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                | Implemented: overview, events, discounts, and receipts own their data and actions; obsolete fragment/tab compatibility is deleted.                                                                                                                              |\n+| D-007 | Registration and transfer Checkout scope | A new registration and its add-ons use one Stripe Checkout Session. Transfers use the same review pattern but remain a fixed bundle with recipient eligibility, questions, current prices, and discounts rechecked.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         | Implemented: registration/add-on settlement and fixed-bundle transfer keep distinct post-payment recovery rather than a generic framework.                                                                                                                      |\n+| D-008 | Shared payment accounts                  | One payment account may serve multiple Evorto organizations. No cross-organization uniqueness restriction is required; tenant data, access, events, settings, and payment records remain isolated.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          | Accepted: first attachment remains organization-scoped and exposes readiness only. No cross-organization lookup, uniqueness rule, or compatibility path was added.                                                                                              |\n+\n+## Implementation batches reconstructed in the stack\n+\n+- Removed prior compliance artifacts, dead dependencies, the migration runner,\n+  migration steps, old schema history, and the generated legacy snapshot.\n+- Made local database targeting and seeding explicit and fail closed; hardened\n+  provider fixtures, tenant assets, runtime state, and the production image.\n+- Enforced the registration graph; settled registration and add-ons in one\n+  Checkout; rebuilt private transfer claims, refund recovery, and recipient\n+  acquisition checks; removed direct participant reassignment.\n+- Added narrow first-payment-account attachment and serialization, with a\n+  private operations entry point and no client-visible account identifier.\n+- Added the new default theme while retaining both prior themes.\n+- Made client failures plain and explicit; simplified shared forms; tightened\n+  access, scanner, QR, tenant-address, role, identity, and onboarding behavior.\n+- Replaced shared deployment state and rollback paths with isolated,\n+  forward-only Scaleway releases and explicit configuration.\n+- Split settings and profile into focused pages; strengthened role/member\n+  administration and profile identity validation; deleted unused user state.\n+- Rechecked registration eligibility at every write and refunded paid access\n+  when eligibility changes.\n+- Completed template authoring, removed obsolete template APIs/forms, made\n+  templates structure-only, derived ordinary discovery from sign-up choices,\n+  and targeted information-only events by explicit roles.\n+- Rebuilt receipt evidence, finance writes and views, reimbursement policy,\n+  email single-dispatch behavior, and the outbox overview.\n+\n+## Final verification ledger\n+\n+| Gate                                             | State at prepared checkpoint | Completion record                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         |\n+| ------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n+| Format                                           | Passed                       | `bun run format:write` on `3e8dba22`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      |\n+| Lint                                             | Passed                       | `bun run lint` on `3e8dba22`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n+| Release-source checks                            | Passed                       | 4/4 focused checks                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |\n+| Server unit                                      | Passed                       | 186/186 files, 1,484/1,484 tests, zero incomplete                                                                                                                                                                                                                         |\n+| Production build                                 | Passed                       | Browser, server-rendered app, and operations bundles                                                                                                                                                                                                                      |\n+| UI replay and application unit                   | **PENDING**                  | Replay the focused UI/test layers, then record the complete zero-failure, zero-incomplete result. Current source-only result is 127/133 files and 950/961 tests.                                                                                                          |\n+| Docker lifecycle and runtime image               | **PENDING**                  | Apply the bounded lifecycle slice, perform a project-scoped clean start and state-preserving resume, prove bounded failure diagnostics, readiness, image contents, and security results. Do not reset unrelated projects.                                                 |\n+| PostgreSQL                                       | **PENDING**                  | Record the full current-tree suite, including registration/payment/transfer concurrency, discovery/role integrity, attachment serialization, receipt, and email cases.                                                                                                    |\n+| Playwright, generated guides, and live providers | **PENDING**                  | Record complete functional and integration suites, official guide generation/publication and asset audit, live membership-card certification, and current map behavior. Missing credentials must stop visibly; no mock, stale output, or partial publication substitutes. |\n+| In-app Browser                                   | **PENDING**                  | Record branch-authentic walkthroughs separately from Playwright: option-derived discovery, anonymous direct-link behavior, explicit ineligibility, announcement role targeting, the default theme, and changed critical flows.                                            |\n+\n+Every collected final suite must have zero failures, skips, todos, fixmes,\n+expected failures, retries, flakes, interruptions, or focused tests. The\n+cancelled repository scan remains cancelled and is not part of this proof.\n+\n+## Closure condition\n+\n+RQ-015 and every proof-dependent coverage row remain **In progress** until the\n+pending records above contain observed final-tree results. Before marking this\n+queue complete:\n+\n+1. Replay the remaining UI and bounded Docker slices on top of source checkpoint\n+   `3e8dba22` and preserve focused, human-reviewable pull requests.\n+2. Run every pending gate on the unchanged final tree.\n+3. Replace each **PENDING** record with its exact result, final commit, and tree.\n+4. Recheck that no compatibility alias, silent fallback, user-facing technical\n+   wording, or generic framework was introduced during the final replay.\n+5. Keep Browser acceptance separate from automated evidence.\n+\n+If a gate fails or an external prerequisite is absent, keep the corresponding\n+row in progress or blocked with the exact reason. Do not copy historical proof\n+from the former PR branch and do not call the application-review queue closed.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019fd2d8-aa27-7b33-9da1-34e7e79b653d"}}}
